{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/930003-mixed-magic","id":930003,"title":"Mixed Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-11T15:45:39-07:00","id":930003,"title":"Mixed Magic","content":"For anyone that's experimented with crossovers, has anyone played with the idea of what would happen if two magic systems were overlapped. Not like making abominations, but like &quot;what would happen if a tremere thaumaturge and a fallen maleficar tried to create a ritual together&quot;. What would happen? What could they do together that neither can accomplish separately? What could be the possible consequences?<br /> <br /> It was always a cool concept to throw around in my games, so was wondering if anyone else tried it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T05:14:46-07:00","id":931935,"title":"","content":"There are no hard and fast rules for it, but theoretically it's either as limited as the least-flexible mechanic or as varied as the most flexible. A lot of it comes down to house ruling - how much do you want it to accomplish? Such things are likely more plot devices than anything else.<br /> <br /> One thing I do believe is that it would be far more difficult to dispel such an effect - a vampire can make a ward that can be scrubbed away by anything that can go through it and wipe away the blood, and a mage can dispel a Correspondence barrier, but incorporating the two effects allows the blood to be harder to wipe off, and the barrier to be more static and harder to violate with just magic. Combining multiple sources of power (vampire, werewolf, mage, and demonic, say) allows you to build impressive effects.<br /> <br /> At the far end, you have the potential (potential, mind, not guarantee) to do something truly impressive - I think this was the idea behind the Red Sign adventure (Mages and Vampires working together to try and overcome the Vampiric curse). Alternatively, you could make it so that only an effect that all parties can achieve is achieved, but make it more resilient (as above - many supernaturals can make a barrier of some sort, so they could work together to strengthen the barrier; but, a Thaumaturge who doesn't have any kind of spatial manipulation magic couldn't contribute to a portal designed by a Mage and Garou based around Correspondence and Moon Bridge rites respectively).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T11:42:56-07:00","id":932119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/930003-mixed-magic?p=931935#post931935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no hard and fast rules for it, but theoretically it's either as limited as the least-flexible mechanic or as varied as the most flexible. A lot of it comes down to house ruling - how much do you want it to accomplish? Such things are likely more plot devices than anything else.<br /> <br /> One thing I do believe is that it would be far more difficult to dispel such an effect - a vampire can make a ward that can be scrubbed away by anything that can go through it and wipe away the blood, and a mage can dispel a Correspondence barrier, but incorporating the two effects allows the blood to be harder to wipe off, and the barrier to be more static and harder to violate with just magic. Combining multiple sources of power (vampire, werewolf, mage, and demonic, say) allows you to build impressive effects.<br /> <br /> At the far end, you have the potential (potential, mind, not guarantee) to do something truly impressive - I think this was the idea behind the Red Sign adventure (Mages and Vampires working together to try and overcome the Vampiric curse). Alternatively, you could make it so that only an effect that all parties can achieve is achieved, but make it more resilient (as above - many supernaturals can make a barrier of some sort, so they could work together to strengthen the barrier; but, a Thaumaturge who doesn't have any kind of spatial manipulation magic couldn't contribute to a portal designed by a Mage and Garou based around Correspondence and Moon Bridge rites respectively).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Exactly! Though I would allow for the two parties to achieve an effect neither could feasibly do on their own(like a garou and a changeling creating a door between the middle umbra and the dreaming), but such effects would require long, difficult rituals as well as rare ingredients and artifacts to act as emulsifiers to contain and blend the two forms of magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}